---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy policy">
  <div class="screen legal-page">
    <div class="page-head reveal">
      <div>
        <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
        <p>Last updated 5 November 2026.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <article class="legal grow scroll">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>From your Google profile: your name, email address, account id and profile picture link.</li>
        <li>Google access and refresh tokens for read-only Gmail access, encrypted at rest.</li>
        <li>Plugins you create, and which plugins are on your list and turned on.</li>
        <li>
          Answers to plugin questions about your new emails, plus short matched text for plugins that use rules.
          Each match is at most 200 characters.
        </li>
        <li>Gmail message and history ids, so no email is answered twice.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How we use your email</h2>
      <p>
        Iris checks for new mail every few minutes, only while at least one plugin is turned on. Each email is read
        on our servers, answered by a model that runs there, and then dropped. We never store email headers or
        whole bodies. Your email is not sent to third-party AI services, is not used to train models, and is not
        read by people. Logs hold ids, never email content.
      </p>

      <h2>Who sees your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          When you turn a plugin on, its developer receives the answers for emails that arrive while it is on,
          along with your email address and username. Each switch asks you first.
        </li>
        <li>A developer can add a plugin to your list by your email address. It stays off until you turn it on.</li>
        <li>We do not sell your data or use it for ads.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          Answers are deleted 30 days after they are made once the developer has fetched them, or once the
          plugin is removed from your list. All answers are deleted after 100 days.
        </li>
        <li>Deleting a plugin deletes its answers.</li>
        <li>
          Deleting your account revokes Iris's Google access and deletes your account, tokens, plugins and answers
          right away.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Turn a plugin off, or remove it, on <a href="/subscriptions">your subscriptions page</a>.</li>
        <li>Delete your account from the same page.</li>
        <li>
          Revoke access at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google account permissions</a>. Iris
          then turns your plugins off.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Google user data</h2>
      <p>
        Iris's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>We use only the cookies needed to keep you signed in and protect forms. No tracking or analytics.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We will update this page and its date when this policy changes.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Iris is created and run by Sreyash Satpathy. Email <a href="mailto:f20250721@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in">f20250721@pilani.bits-pilani.ac.in</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
